# 19. NON-NEGOTIABLE DEVELOPMENT RULES

1. Do not build a frontend-only mockup.
2. Do not create buttons that do nothing.
3. Do not use fake API responses in the completed application.
4. Do not fabricate model training or performance.
5. Do not claim that a dataset contains theft labels when it does not.
6. Do not invent official integrations.
7. Do not expose API keys.
8. Do not send sensitive data to LLM providers without appropriate privacy controls.
9. Do not let an LLM make final emergency or law-enforcement decisions.
10. Do not remove existing working functionality without justification.
11. Do not leave critical functionality as TODO comments.
12. Do not stop after writing documentation.
13. Do not report a feature as completed until it has been tested.
14. Do not hide failures behind mock data.
15. Prefer a smaller number of fully working features over many incomplete features.

If a capability is blocked by Android restrictions, unavailable APIs, missing permissions, or unavailable datasets, explain the limitation and implement the safest valid alternative.

